1
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,690
Ah! Miss Stewart! Welcome!

2
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:15,540
How are you?

3
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:16,990
Fine, Somsak. And you?

4
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:18,310
Fine, thank you.

5
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:20,380
This is my friend Harry Bennett.

6
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,260
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,570
Very nice to meet you.

8
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:25,500
Any friend of Miss Stewart's is welcome at Somsak's.

9
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,920
Follow me, please.

10
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,890
I like it here.

11
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:32,990
I do, too. I come here often.

12
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:35,680
A special place for special people.

13
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:39,430
Thank you, Somsak.

14
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:45,770
Well! Nice restaurant.

15
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:47,040
Would you like something to drink?

16
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,730
Yes, I'd like a glass of ginger ale with ice.

17
00:00:49,730 --> 00:00:52,140
Harry, what would you like?

18
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:54,020
Do you have a dry white wine?

19
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:55,540
How about a California chablis?

20
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,460
Chablis is fine.

21
00:00:57,460 --> 00:00:59,600
What would you like to eat?

22
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,590
I'd like the mee krob.

23
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:03,470
Harry, would you like to see a menu?

24
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:04,420
No, it's Ok.

25
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:09,960
I'll have the mee krob also.

26
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,340
What is it?

27
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,800
Crispy fried noodles. I love them.

28
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,060
May I bring you a salad?

29
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:18,200
Oh yes.

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,650
What do you recommend today?

31
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:21,710
I recommend rose-petal salad.

32
00:01:21,710 --> 00:01:24,650
Special for new friends.

33
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:26,510
Rose-petal salad?

34
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:28,210
Why not?

35
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:33,380
I'll take care of everything.

36
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:36,180
I hope you're hungry.

37
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:43,750
What? Oh, yes. Starving. Well, I...

38
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:47,710
Well, I ...

39
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:50,100
What do you do at Universe Toy Company?

40
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,030
I'm the vice-president of new toy development.

41
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,940
Terrific!

42
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,480
I know you 're a CPA.

43
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,310
That's true. Harry Bennett,

44
00:01:59,310 --> 00:02:01,250
certified public accountant.

45
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,980
I love numbers.

46
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:04,040
I do some work for Smith and Dale,

47
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,040
Your company's accounting firm.

48
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:09,400
And so...

49
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,940
Here we are.

50
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,510
Yes.

51
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:13,680
I have a daughter.

52
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,990
I know. How old is she?

53
00:02:15,990 --> 00:02:17,440
She's nine years old.

54
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:19,500
That's a nice age. What's her name?

55
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:20,980
Michelle.

56
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:33,420
Do you have a picture of her?

57
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,790
She's very pretty.

58
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:43,380
Thank you.

59
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:46,050
Rose-petal salad.

60
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:49,500
And there's a phone call for you, Mr. Bennett.

61
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,310
Excuse me, Susan.

62
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:54,850
I hope nothing is wrong.

63
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:56,160
I'll get the rest of the dinner.

64
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:10,330
Excuse me.

65
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:12,260
Please forgive me, Susan, but...

66
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:16,560
I have to leave. I feel terrible, but...

67
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,290
What's the matter?

68
00:03:18,290 --> 00:03:20,150
My daughter isn't feeling well.

69
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:22,660
Oh no! Is it serious?

70
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:26,510
I don't know. The baby-sitter says she has a stomachache,

71
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:27,360
and she's crying.

72
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,080
I'll have to go home.

73
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,010
Will you forgive me?

74
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:33,050
Of course. I'm so sorry for Michelle.

75
00:03:33,050 --> 00:03:34,850
And you didn't have a chance to eat.

76
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:36,310
Oh, it's OK.

77
00:03:36,310 --> 00:03:37,530
Let me take you home first.

78
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:40,070
No, no. Please, go ahead.

79
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:42,080
It's our first date.

80
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,620
We'll make another.

81
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:46,540
Please don't worry.

82
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:47,460
I'll phone you.

83
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:51,430
I hope your daughter is all right. Good-bye.

84
00:03:51,430 --> 00:03:54,430
Good-bye.
